<title>USA: Sept Brent crude slides in late US paper trading.</title>
<headline>Sept Brent crude slides in late US paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>September Brent crude oil slid in late U.S. paper trading on Monday, trader said.</p>
<p>A string of partial September cargoes switched hands at $17.78 and $17.80 a barrel, compared to the IPE settlement of $17.86 a barrel.</p>
<p>August/September Brent traded at minus eight cents a barrel, down a penny from the day's earlier transactions.</p>
<p>September/October Brent was assessed at minus 12/14 cents a barrel.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
